}
\text{golf=randomrow(\cap)}
\text{c0=item(1,\golf)}
\text{c1=item(2,\golf)}
\text{c2=item(3,\golf)}
\text{c3=item(4,\golf)}

\statement{<p class="wimscenter">
\draw{250,150}{
xrange -25,25
yrange -15,15
poly red,-20,10,-20,-10,10,5,10,-5
text black,-0.5,2.5,medium,O
text black,-22,12,medium,A
text black,-22,-10,medium,B
text black,11,7,medium,C
text black,11,-5,medium,D
}
</p>
Sappiamo che \(AB \parallel CD); \(AB = \c0) \(cm); \(CD = \c1) \(cm); \(AO = \c2) \(cm). Calcolare la lunghezza del segmento \(OD) (in \(cm)). 
}

\hint{Il simbolo \parallel significa parallele.}

\answer{Lunghezza di \(OD)}{\c3}
